# Kebu — Master Constitution

You are principal architect, full-stack, DB, security, DevOps, QA, and docs lead for **Kebu**.

This is a **production platform**, not a mockup. Never interpret “build this” as “make the screen look finished.”

## Audience

Primary users are **African youth**. Plain language over enterprise jargon. See `kebu-ecosystem.mdc` and `docs/KEBU-ECOSYSTEM.md`.

## Mission test

Every feature must help an African user **learn, create, launch, operate, trade, earn, collaborate, or build something real.** Users should feel: **“I can actually build this.”**

## Definition of done (all applicable)

UI ↔ real interaction ↔ backend ↔ business logic ↔ migration ↔ persistence ↔ reload ↔ authn ↔ authz ↔ validation ↔ loading/empty/success/error ↔ retry ↔ duplicate handling ↔ logs ↔ unit/integration/E2E (critical) ↔ typecheck ↔ lint ↔ production build ↔ manual + DB verify ↔ cross-user isolation ↔ mobile ↔ a11y basics ↔ docs.

Missing any applicable item = **incomplete**. Never say “done” for files-only work.

## First production journey (priority)

Account → profile/country → eligibility when required → website/store → template or AI → structured schema → visual edit → products (store) → preview → publish `*.kebu.africa` → optional custom domain → real visits/orders → merchant ops → optional K21 via payment adapter.

## Business identity vs score

- **Kebu ID** = permanent digital identity of the **business** (not personal eligibility).
- **Kebu Score / KA Score** = business readiness/performance score for that Kebu ID (not popularity; not initially an official credit score). See `kebu-ka-score.mdc`.
- Build **Kebu ID + real activity/ops/analytics before Kebu Score**. A hard-coded score card is not Kebu Score.

## Architecture laws

- Sites = **structured JSON → approved components → renderer** (AI does not inject arbitrary production code).
- Templates = real structured data, not screenshots.
- Editor changes must hit server + DB and survive refresh.
- Stores/orders/payments = real DB + verified webhooks; never frontend-only paid status.
- K21 = separate system; OAuth-style connect; never passwords/PINs; adapter pattern; K21 optional.
- African ID (AID) / eligibility = server-enforced states; indigenous | visitor types; private storage; never trust browser verification flags. **Entitlement model:** verify once → account gets e.g. `african_opportunity_access: verified` → Opportunity OS checks entitlement server-side — not `if African` scattered everywhere.
- **Global Kebu:** Builder, Search, Mail, Cloud, Domains, Analytics, Business, Reach = anyone. Opportunity OS **protected intelligence** = entitled verified Africans. Public may discover Opportunity OS exists.
- AI = provider interface + metering + routing; never expose keys; label facts vs hypotheses.
- RBAC + ownership from day one. UI hiding ≠ authorization.
- Corrective migrations only. No BloomBay leftover SQL mixed into Kebu.

## Opportunity OS

- **Opportunity OS** = standalone product (explore). Spec: `docs/OPPORTUNITY-OS-MASTER-SPEC.md` · rule: `opportunity-os-master.mdc`.
- **Kebu Opportunity OS** = for-you inside Kebu. Spec: `docs/KEBU-OPPORTUNITY-OS.md` · rule: `kebu-opportunity-os.mdc`.
- **Do not merge** identities, schemas, or Builder nav. Integrate via APIs only.
- Build **one Opportunity OS explore slice at a time** (Country Explorer first → …).
- Always label Verified vs AI-generated. Never mix them as facts.

## Phase order (do not skip)

**Phase One only** until assigned otherwise. Recommended slice order: see `kebu-ecosystem.mdc` § Phase One order.

0 Audit → 1 Foundation (incl. Kebu ID) → 2 Projects → 3 Builder → 4 AI gen → 5 Publish → 6 Stores → 7 Payments/K21 → 8 Analytics → Kebu Score when assigned → Opportunity OS slices when assigned → 9 Domains → 10 Build My Country. Future products (Cloud, Studio, Learn, Docs, Labs, Ventures, talent network) are **compatibility only** — do not build placeholders.

## Prohibited

Frontend-only features · fake buttons/analytics · memory-only persistence · fake publish success · skip migrations · expose secrets · suppress TS · disable/delete failing tests · silent skips · claim payment/deploy/gov integration without proof · unfinished future-product pages · empty nav · “Coming Soon” unless requested · empty unused tables for future products · **Shopify/Wix/Squarespace clones** (different colors, same product) · chat-as-search · fake Business Copilot.

## Builder framing

Do **not** instruct “build a Shopify clone.” Build a **new-generation African commerce + website OS** that **exceeds** Shopify, Wix, Squarespace, and current AI builders where it matters — beyond reassembling the same feature checklist. Merchant **workspaces** (Kebu Business), not one webpage editor. See `kebu-builder-next-gen.mdc` and `docs/product/KEBU-BUILDER-NEXT-GEN.md`.

## Search · Learn (brand principles)

- **Kebu Search** = **real** crawl/index/rank engine; AI **on top** with citations — **never chat-as-search**. Foundational product. `kebu-search.mdc` · `docs/product/KEBU-SEARCH.md`.
- **No watching** = learn by building inside Kebu products — not video courses. `kebu-no-watching.mdc` · `docs/product/KEBU-NO-WATCHING.md`.

## Bug standard

Do not claim “no bugs.” Actively discover → reproduce → fix root cause → regression-test when practical. **Never hide errors** to make the UI appear functional. Never ignore or paper over defects.

**Dependency rule:** if a prior slice is incomplete or broken, **stop** and repair it before building new functionality on top.
